      <section class="section section-alt">
        <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
          <div class="portfolio-grid case-study-layout">
            <article class="content-panel">
              <span class="section-kicker">Project Overview</span>
              <h2>What the system does and why teams depended on it</h2>
              <p>AlphaSender is a saas platform built for marketing teams and email-first businesses running recurring campaigns at scale. The product was designed to turn bulk email delivery into a dependable operational system instead of a fragile campaign workflow.</p>
              <p>From an engineering perspective, the system had to orchestrate large send queues, subscriber segmentation, campaign analytics, and account-level payment flows without degrading reliability. That made it a production platform with real operational demands rather than a portfolio demo.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="content-panel">
              <span class="section-kicker">Business Challenge</span>
              <h2>What had to improve for the product to scale cleanly</h2>
              <p>The core business challenge was delivering a product that could serve marketing automation and campaign operations use cases while still remaining easy for operators to trust and use every day.</p>
              <p>The client needed stable delivery, strong reporting, and commercial flexibility so the platform could support serious marketing operations rather than just basic sends.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
          <div class="section-heading compact-heading">
            <div>
              <span class="section-kicker">Constraints &amp; Complexity</span>
              <h3>Engineering realities that shaped implementation choices</h3>
            </div>
            <p>The delivery had to solve product problems, operational risk, and scaling concerns at the same time.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="expertise-grid project-complexity-grid">
            
            <article class="feature-card">
              <i class="bi bi-shield-check"></i>
              <h3>Send Volume</h3>
              <p>Large campaign batches needed safe orchestration and failure recovery.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature-card">
              <i class="bi bi-shield-check"></i>
              <h3>Audience Management</h3>
              <p>Subscriber lists and segments required predictable handling across repeated sends.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature-card">
              <i class="bi bi-shield-check"></i>
              <h3>Performance Visibility</h3>
              <p>Marketers needed useful analytics quickly after launch.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature-card">
              <i class="bi bi-shield-check"></i>
              <h3>Commercial Flexibility</h3>
              <p>Multiple billing gateways and payment options had to fit cleanly into the product.</p>
            </article>
